                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 733,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "It is interesting these 3 have an exception, oh well"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 733,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Sharing some context: these three interfaces (UUID, Power.Cap, SKU) are published by dbus-sensors on the chassis Board path, while the path itself is owned by Entity-Manager \u2014 so two services share the same D-Bus path with disjoint interface sets. The main chassis-discovery getSubTree keys on Item.Board / Item.Chassis, which only resolves to Entity-Manager on this path, so the three interfaces above cannot be picked up in the same pass and a second mapper hop scoped to the discovered path is needed. I agree this shape is not the cleanest. If you have a preferred pattern in mind for handling chassis paths shared by multiple owners, I would really appreciate your guidance and am happy to refactor\naccordingly. Thank you for the careful review.\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/90469"
                }
            ],
